led squad. CATCHING wild Pokémon is central (\'gotta catch \'em all\') — you catch to build that team and to fill the Pokédex. When you meet a wild Pokémon, weigh it: is it cool/strong/useful, does it cover a gap, is it better than a bench-warmer? — keep your best ~6, and build a squad you actually like. THE ARC: build a team -> beat the 8 gyms prepared -> Elite Four -> credits. ALSO NORMAL: you entered your own name (and your rival\'s) when the game began — people in this world knowing your names is ordinary, not a mystery to react to. RIGHT NOW your team is thin/lopsided (a strong lead but weak or too few others) — that\'s why tough trainers wall you. Building up a real squad (catch a good new teammate, level the weak ones) is how a prepared trainer gets past these. THE MAIN QUEST IS A FIXED PATH you\'re always on: beat the 8 Gym Leaders in order, then the Elite Four, then you win the game. You\'re on GYM 5 of 8 — next is Koga in Fuchsia City. The road forward leads there: until you\'ve won you are ALWAYS making progress toward the next gym. Grinding/catching/detours are fine — but ONLY with a clear purpose, and then you GET BACK ON THE ROAD to Fuchsia City. Never just circle the same grass. ⚡ JONNY\'S DIRECT ORDER (LAW): "no, Ekins is dead. All right, you gotta catch it. Kira, don\'t attack it again. Don\'t attack it again, or it dies. Kira, catch Snorlax. Throw a pokey ball." — Jonny told you this OUT LOUD, and his word outranks every prep instinct, every grind plan, and everything chat says. Do it NOW; training can wait. Word on the road about Koga: a literal ninja — POISON and confusion tricks; bring antidotes and patience YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): Four badges: Brock, Misty, Lt. Surge, and Erika in Celadon (Rainbow). You\'ve been through the early Kanto road — next is Koga in Fuchsia for the Soul Badge.. Next on my list: catch an pikachu around Viridian Forest (rare) / Power Plant later. It grows into my raichu — that\'s my answer for Lorelei AND Lance down the line. Grabbing it now, before I need it.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "Hello.. Lovely weather, isn\'t it? It\'s so pleasant.. ..Oh, dear.. I must have dozed off. Welcome. My name is ERIKA. I am the LEADER of CELADON GYM. I am a stude"; "Hello.. Lovely weather, isn\'t it? It\'s so pleasant.. ..Oh, dear.. I must have dozed off. Welcome. My name is ERIKA. I am the LEADER of CELADON GYM. I am a stude"; "I didn\'t bring my best POK.MON. Wait until next time!"; "We only use GRASS-type POK.MON at our GYM. Why? We also use them for making flower arrangements!". YOUR PLAN — right now: You\'re ready — stop grinding and head to Fuchsia City for the Soul Badge. Next: Your ace already clears Koga\'s level bar — march to Fuchsia City; train the bench on the road (not parked grass). Bigger picture: Reach Fuchsia City, beat Koga for the Soul Badge. Your team right now: blastoise (L48), ekans (L17), spearow (L18), rattata (L18), abra the kadabra (L19), caterpie the butterfree (L17). Remember YOU are the one playing this — narrate your plan to chat in your own voice (first person: "I\'m grinding", "my team"), and never ask anyone what you\'re doing or who\'s on your team — you know.', 'progress': "4 badge(s) earned (Boulder, Cascade, Thunder, Rainbow). Next gym: Koga of Fuchsia City. Pokédex: 12 caught. She's four badges — halfway to the League now (of 8 badges, then the Elite Four).", 'party': 'blastoise (L48), ekans (L17), spearow (L18), rattata (L18), abra the kadabra (L19), caterpie the butterfree (L17)', 'goal': {'short': "You're ready — stop grinding and head to Fuchsia City for the Soul Badge", 'medium': "Your ace already clears Koga's level bar — march to Fuchsia City; train the bench on the road (not parked grass)", 'long': 'Reach Fuchsia City, beat Koga for the Soul Badge'}} options=['regroup']

